{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Speak, etc.</b> The meaning is: and if it were on account of that when YHWH speaks with us we accept His decrees — from now on, behold, we accept from you, and if so there is no need for the thing; so why should we place ourselves in danger? And this is what it says, <b>lest we die.</b> It further intends along this line: <b>You speak with us and we will hear</b> — meaning, there will be power in us to hear; but if YHWH speaks with us — lest we die and not hear."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:31:12.317860040Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}